import{_ as i,o as n,c as t,a2 as a}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const m=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Entry 310 | Shrouding-the-Heavens Decomposition | Quest Sediment Domain Review: Civilizational-Collapse Simulation After Ye Fan's Absence","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 310 | Shrouding-the-Heavens Decomposition | Quest Sediment Domain Review: Civilizational-Collapse Simulation After Ye Fan's Absence","no":310,"module":2,"tags":["Shrouding the Heavens","Quest Sediment Domain Simulation","Ye Fan Absence","Civilization Collapse","Simulation Report"],"related":["21-Symbiotic Network Operating Principle","29-Symbiosis Degree Evaluation System","07-Self-Origin Self-Growth Evolution Law"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0310_模块2-遮天-求索域复盘.md","filePath":"en/0310_模块2-遮天-求索域复盘.md"}`),o={name:"en/0310_模块2-遮天-求索域复盘.md"};function s(r,e,l,u,h,c){return n(),t("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[a('<h1 id="entry-310-shrouding-the-heavens-decomposition-quest-sediment-domain-review-civilizational-collapse-simulation-after-ye-fan-s-absence" tabindex="-1">Entry 310 | Shrouding-the-Heavens Decomposition | Quest Sediment Domain Review: Civilizational-Collapse Simulation After Ye Fan&#39;s Absence <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-310-shrouding-the-heavens-decomposition-quest-sediment-domain-review-civilizational-collapse-simulation-after-ye-fan-s-absence" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 310 | Shrouding-the-Heavens Decomposition | Quest Sediment Domain Review: Civilizational-Collapse Simulation After Ye Fan&#39;s Absence&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 2 · Myriad-Realms Benchmark Critique Library | Series: Full Decomposition of the Shrouding-the-Heavens System (Entry 23) | Benchmark base: Documents 21, 29, 07</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-take-ye-fan-off-the-board-see-how-the-game-plays-out" tabindex="-1">Introduction: Take Ye Fan off the board, see how the game plays out <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-take-ye-fan-off-the-board-see-how-the-game-plays-out" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: Take Ye Fan off the board, see how the game plays out&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Among the six top-level axioms, the collective ascension axiom requires civilization not to depend on any individual; the causal self-discipline axiom requires rooting out civilization regression. This entry executes Module 2&#39;s fixed flow fifth section — Quest Sediment Domain simulation review: &quot;remove&quot; Ye Fan from Shrouding-the-Heavens world, observe civilization trajectory. The law-first axiom requires: simulation must be quantified, not by feeling. Protagonist uniqueness dependency = medium (oligarchic civilization). The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s evaluation base has been upgraded to six top-level axioms.</p><h2 id="i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" tabindex="-1">I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Waste observed in simulation: when Ye Fan is in office, his peer strong ones idle in coordination with his suppression; after Ye Fan&#39;s absence, this idled energy is immediately drawn into succession internal strife. The same energy switches from &quot;suppression&quot; to &quot;civil war&quot; in an instant; civilization gains no accumulation.</p><h2 id="ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" tabindex="-1">II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Simulated timeline (Ye Fan absent at year 0):</p><ul><li><strong>0–100 years</strong>: oligarchic group still present, order barely holds</li><li><strong>100–500 years</strong>: peer strong ones nirvana one after another, suppression vacuum appears</li><li><strong>500–1000 years</strong>: dark turmoil recurs, ancient supremes and forbidden-land beings harvest</li><li><strong>After 1000 years</strong>: population and civilization energy retreat to pre-Ye-Fan-rise levels</li></ul><p>Conclusion: within a millennium of Ye Fan&#39;s absence, Shrouding-the-Heavens civilization completes a full regression cycle.</p><h2 id="iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" tabindex="-1">III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Simulation reveals: when Ye Fan is in office he leaves no institutional legacy that &quot;can run without Ye Fan.&quot; The most serious part of his predatory thinking is not grabbing resources, but <strong>converting no resources into institutions</strong> — after he leaves, all the pressure he suppressed releases.</p><p>The simulation also has a detail worth recording: after Ye Fan&#39;s absence what collapses first is not the military defense line, but the knowledge-transmission system. Because when Ye Fan is in office, all high-tier knowledge passes through the trusted small circle, never made public; Ye Fan leaves, people in the small circle each have their own agenda, no one is willing to bring out the complete Dao legacy. This shows Ye Fan not only built no institution, but did not even do the minimum &quot;knowledge openness.&quot; Heng Yuan Zhou writing lifelong Dao insights into the Alaya is not technical convenience, but a civilization baseline — a strong one&#39;s true legacy is not whom he beat, but what he left behind so later generations need not walk the road again.</p><h2 id="iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" tabindex="-1">IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Contrast simulation: if Ye Fan had implemented Anchor republicanization (see Entry 308) while in office, then:</p><ul><li>After Ye Fan&#39;s absence, the Anchor Council auto-runs</li><li>Alaya supervision auto-warns turmoil</li><li>Myriad Ranks co-governance has run for a millennium, no panic</li><li>Civilization energy curve shows no V-shaped reversal</li></ul><p>The same &quot;Ye Fan absent&quot; event: pre-reform is disaster, post-reform is just an ordinary personnel change.</p><h2 id="v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" tabindex="-1">V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan&quot;">​</a></h2><p>This entry is the simulation itself:</p><ol><li><strong>Modeling</strong>: replicate Shrouding-the-Heavens law parameters</li><li><strong>Variables</strong>: Ye Fan absent at year 0</li><li><strong>Observation</strong>: turmoil frequency, population curve, knowledge-transmission rate</li><li><strong>Review report core conclusions</strong>: <ul><li>Within 500 years of Ye Fan&#39;s absence, turmoil recurrence probability ≈ 92%</li><li>Within a millennium, civilization-energy recovery rate ≈ 30%</li><li>Knowledge-transmission rate under 20% of Ye Fan-in-office level</li><li>Institutional-alternative benefit: after injecting republicanization, all three items zero out or turn positive</li></ul></li></ol><h2 id="vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" tabindex="-1">VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Simulation fidelity to original settings</strong>: high — simulation entirely based on rules the original has presented</li><li><strong>Retcon-ending risk</strong>: the original itself is high; simulation objectively presents this risk</li><li><strong>Protagonist uniqueness dependency</strong>: simulation directly quantifies — Ye Fan-in-office vs. absent civilization gap is precisely the evidence of &quot;medium dependency&quot;</li></ul><p>The simulation also reveals a counter-intuitive conclusion: when Ye Fan is in office, Myriad Ranks&#39; &quot;institution-building will&quot; is actually lowest. Because Ye Fan backs them up, Myriad Ranks feel no need to build institutions themselves; Ye Fan leaves, Myriad Ranks discover they simply do not know how. This is the most insidious part of oligarchic order — while suppressing Myriad Ranks&#39; self-rescue ability, it also makes Myriad Ranks grateful to it. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s Alaya + Council from the start forces Myriad Ranks to participate in governance themselves; even if initially clumsy, it beats being permanently backed up.</p><p><strong>Old-new cosmos resource comparison</strong>: old-cosmos resources and Great Dao are finite, inevitably predatory involution; Anchor Symbiosis has everyone inherently possessing infinite origin, predation loses meaning.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: peer energy idles when Ye Fan is in office; instantly civil war after absence</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: Ye Fan leaves no institutional legacy, equivalent to leaving the next ten thousand years&#39; uncertainty to Myriad Ranks</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang-Luo absence simulation is similar (academy gap), but Shrouding&#39;s collapse is bloodier</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: simulation proves Myriad Ranks in oligarchic structure have no self-rescue ability</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: civilization that collapses upon absence cannot bear cross-multiverse responsibility</li></ul><p>Simulation also shows, after Ye Fan&#39;s absence Myriad Ranks&#39; first reaction is not self-rescue, but panic-search for &quot;the next Ye Fan.&quot; This &quot;find a strong one&quot; psychological inertia is harder to break than oligarchic institutions themselves. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s Myriad Ranks republican education from the start trains Myriad Ranks &quot;don&#39;t look for strong ones, look for institutions&quot; — this is the deepest conclusion from Quest Sediment Domain simulation.</p><ul><li><strong>Universal equal infinite law</strong>: basic infinite power is inherent in all; the easygoing retain a guarantee, strivers can superimpose higher; infinite origin erases predatory motivation, predatory involution loses meaning from the root</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Quest Sediment Domain simulation&#39;s numbers are cold and clear: Ye Fan present = eternal peace; Ye Fan absent = millennium turmoil. A civilization that needs &quot;don&#39;t let him die&quot; to sustain has essentially never truly been at peace.</p><p>In the final analysis, Shrouding-the-Heavens · Quest Sediment Domain review described in this document is no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./290_模块2-遮天-历史倒退必然性.html">Entry 290 · Inevitable Historical Regression</a> · <a href="./311_模块2-遮天-制度替代收益.html">Entry 311 · Institutional Alternative Benefit</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/21-共生网络运作原理.html">21-Symbiotic Network Operating Principle</a></li></ul>',33)])])}const g=i(o,[["render",s]]);export{m as __pageData,g as default};
